WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.500
Spatial-Interactor · Learn, interact, reason.

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:18.000
People do not learn space by looking alone.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:29.000
Each action changes the world—and the world answers back.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:40.000
How do we learn space? By moving, acting, and interacting with the world.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:50.000
From local state transitions to long-horizon spatial states.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Learn one step first, then connect the steps.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:10.000
Three stages: passive world changes, active self-motion, and long-trajectory integration.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:20.000
Given a trajectory, how far did the camera move?

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:30.000
Forward, turn left, move forward... can the model recover the complete spatial state?

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:40.000
One interaction becomes the capability for the next.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:45.408
Spatial-Interactor · Understanding space through interaction.
